mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course provides an introduction to natural medicines, systematically covering the fundamental theories and research methods in natural product chemistry. It includes the historical development of the discipline, sources of natural medicines, typical chemical structural types, biosynthetic pathways, and cutting-edge research technologies. Through case studies and literature review, the course aims to help students understand the significance of natural medicines in innovative drug discovery and cultivate interdisciplinary perspectives and innovative abilities in future professionals.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
